reachy-motion-recreation

This project recreates the system described in "The best expressive harness for robots" by Binh Pham
(https://garden.binhph.am/articles/the-best-expressive-harness-for-robots), whose reference implementation is
https://github.com/pham-tuan-binh/reachy-motion-generator (Apache-2.0). Modules under rmr/ are ports of that
implementation and say which file they follow.

Third-party material included here, all Apache-2.0:
- data/teacher/*: the teacher dataset, validation set, seed recipes and evaluation prompts from
  pham-tuan-binh/reachy-motion-generator (distill_data/ and planner/examples/).
- rmr/assets/kinematics_data.json: from pollen-robotics/reachy_mini.
- visualizer/: adapted from pham-tuan-binh/reachy-motion-generator (visualizer/). Its 3D model, meshes
  (visualizer/assets/), scene and passive-joint kinematics come from
  https://huggingface.co/spaces/8bitkick/reachy_mini_3d_web_viz (visualizer/LICENSE-reachy_mini_3d_web_viz.txt);
  visualizer/src/StewartIK.js ports pollen-robotics/reachy_mini_rust_kinematics.
- visualizer/examples/examples.json: includes 12 clips of pollen-robotics/reachy-mini-emotions-library
  (resampled to 25 Hz) for comparison with generated motions.
